{"name":"Hazel Blush","hex":"#eae2de","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hazel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tree or shrub of the genus Corylus, bearing edible nuts called hazelnuts or filberts.","The nut of the hazel tree."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a greenish-brown colour. (often used to refer to eye colour)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hazel"},{"term":"blush","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of blushing; a pink or red glow on the face caused by embarrassment, shame, shyness, love, etc.","A glow; a flush of colour, especially pink or red."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To become red or pink in the face (and sometimes experience an associated feeling of warmth), especially due to shyness, love, shame, excitement, or embarrassment.","To be shy, ashamed, or embarrassed (to do something)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blush"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hazel","blocks":[{"text":"Hazels are plants of the genus Corylus of deciduous trees and large shrubs native to the temperate Northern Hemisphere. The genus is usually placed in the birch family, Betulaceae, though some botanists split the hazels into a separate family Corylaceae. The fruit of the hazel is the hazelnut; the trees are also grown as ornaments in hedges or gardens."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Corylus_avellana_0001.JPG/330px-Corylus_avellana_0001.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hazel","wikidata":"Q145889"},{"title":"Eye color","blocks":[{"text":"Eye color is a polygenic phenotypic trait determined by two factors: the pigmentation of the eye's iris and the frequency-dependence of the scattering of light by the turbid medium in the stroma of the iris."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Farbverlauf_Augenfarben.jpg/330px-Farbverlauf_Augenfarben.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye_color","wikidata":"Q23786"},{"title":"Blush (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Blush is a medium bright tone of pink."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Blush_rose_1.jpg/330px-Blush_rose_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blush_(color)","wikidata":"Q22133966"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Catkins_Corylus_avellana-Mont_Bart-5124~2015_12_26.JPG/500px-Catkins_Corylus_avellana-Mont_Bart-5124~2015_12_26.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Catkins_Corylus_avellana-Mont_Bart-5124~2015_12_26.JPG/1280px-Catkins_Corylus_avellana-Mont_Bart-5124~2015_12_26.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Catkins_Corylus_avellana-Mont_Bart-5124~2015_12_26.JPG/500px-Catkins_Corylus_avellana-Mont_Bart-5124~2015_12_26.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Young male catkins of Corylus avellana","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACatkins_Corylus_avellana-Mont_Bart-5124~2015_12_26.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/%28ms%29_Corylus_colurna_6.jpg/250px-%28ms%29_Corylus_colurna_6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/%28ms%29_Corylus_colurna_6.jpg/500px-%28ms%29_Corylus_colurna_6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/%28ms%29_Corylus_colurna_6.jpg/250px-%28ms%29_Corylus_colurna_6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumb